From 448dbc74da3fc2f5c57ee490a26bd1ae9c1a2b20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 10:02:43 +0200
Subject: [RFC PATCH v4 06/10] iommu/rockchip: Set AUTO_GATING bit 31 on enable

On the RK356x IOMMU, the page-table walker has its own clock that can be
auto-gated. Setting RK_MMU_AUTO_GATING bit 31 before paging is enabled
keeps that clock running, matching the vendor driver's clock-gating
handling (rockchip-linux kernel commits 7f8158fb and 6a355e5f). The
write is a read-modify-write so the register's reset value is preserved.

This is needed by the RK3568 NPU MMU. Note that on current mainline the
page-table walk completes without this write on the boards tested here;
the BSP sets the bit for clock-gating correctness, so it is kept in that
form. IOMMU maintainers may prefer to keep or drop it.

Suggested-by: Chaoyi Chen <chaoyi.chen@rock-chips.com>
Signed-off-by: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
index 4da801369..f7739323c 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/rockchip-iommu.c
@@ -931,6 +931,7 @@ static int rk_iommu_enable(struct rk_iommu *iommu)
 	struct iommu_domain *domain = iommu->domain;
 	struct rk_iommu_domain *rk_domain = to_rk_domain(domain);
 	int ret, i;
+	u32 auto_gate;
 
 	ret = clk_bulk_enable(iommu->num_clocks, iommu->clocks);
 	if (ret)
@@ -949,6 +950,17 @@ static int rk_iommu_enable(struct rk_iommu *iommu)
 			       iommu->rk_ops->mk_dtentries(rk_domain->dt_dma));
 		rk_iommu_base_command(iommu->bases[i], RK_MMU_CMD_ZAP_CACHE);
 		rk_iommu_write(iommu->bases[i], RK_MMU_INT_MASK, RK_MMU_IRQ_MASK);
+
+		/*
+		 * Keep the page-table walker's clock running by setting
+		 * AUTO_GATING bit 31 before paging is enabled, matching the
+		 * vendor driver's clock-gating handling (see rockchip-linux
+		 * kernel commits 7f8158fb and 6a355e5f).  This is a
+		 * read-modify-write so the register's reset value is kept.
+		 */
+		auto_gate = rk_iommu_read(iommu->bases[i], RK_MMU_AUTO_GATING);
+		auto_gate |= BIT(31);
+		rk_iommu_write(iommu->bases[i], RK_MMU_AUTO_GATING, auto_gate);
 	}
 
 	ret = rk_iommu_enable_paging(iommu);
-- 
